Package: bogenplan
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/excelano/bogenplan-desktop
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libegl1, libvulkan1 | libgl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxi6, libxcursor1, libxrandr2, ca-certificates, desktop-file-utils, hicolor-icon-theme
Recommends: gnome-keyring
Description: Your calendars laid out on the Sun's arc
 Bogenplan shows the calendars you keep on iCloud or another CalDAV server
 in Bogenzeit: each day runs from one solar midnight to the next, sunrise
 and sunset sit at fixed heights, and an event's place is read in spans
 before or after solar noon or solar midnight where you are. Civil times
 stay beside every reading.
 .
 It sets moments, zero-length events with an alert at their start, which
 reach every device that has the calendar, and edits or deletes events. Passwords
 are kept in the desktop keyring and events in a private cache, and the only
 network connection is to the calendar server.
